{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5c7eVCDYPhfd7qVeLp8Xm","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nThis adds the daily token check to the pool's claim gate. A job must now pass both the dollar check and the token check. It also adds a once-per-day status-issue notice for each token cap. Both dependencies have landed on main: the dollar gate and its notice loop are in internal/budget, and the token config is in internal/config. The work can start now, and engineer is the only triage role in this repository.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: implementation steps for the token check in internal/budget, wiring it into the existing dollar gate and verdict, the token notice and report, the proposal doc updates, and table tests on a fake clock.\n- worker engineer: Go code, tests and doc changes in internal/budget, the pool wiring and docs/proposal.md.\n\n## Open issues\n- The issue asks for a human review of the claim-rule table and the fail-closed path. eng-review runs on every pull request, but a maintainer should still review those parts of the pull request.\n- No architect or documentation-planner role exists. The engineer's plan has to cover how this fits with the existing dollar gate and notice loop, and the changes to the proposal's Budgets, Configuration, Executors and Reaper sections.\nbudget.go\nbudget_test.go\nnotice.go\nnotice_test.go\ntestdata\n     168 internal/budget/budget.go\n     137 internal/budget/budget_test.go\n     163 internal/budget/notice.go\n     227 internal/budget/notice_test.go\n     695 total\n# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\ninternal/config/defaults.go:132:\t\t\tres.TokensPerDay = int64(*raw.tokensPerDay)\ninternal/config/duration.go:18:// durationToken matches one number-plus-unit component of a duration.\ninternal/config/duration.go:19:var durationToken = regexp.MustCompile(`^([0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]+)?)(ns|us|µs|ms|s|m|h|d|w)`)\ninternal/config/duration.go:35:\t\tm := durationToken.FindStringSubmatch(rest)\ninternal/config/load.go:323:\t\t\tvar tc TokenCount\ninternal/config/load.go:417:\t\trole.TokensPerDay = *ov.tokensPerDay\ninternal/config/raw.go:23:\ttokensPerDay           *TokenCount\ninternal/config/render.go:29:\tTokensPerDay    int64                  `yaml:\"tokens_per_day,omitempty\"`\ninternal/config/render.go:120:\tTokensPerDay    int64   `yaml:\"tokens_per_day,omitempty\"`\ninternal/config/render.go:137:\t\tTokensPerDay:    r.TokensPerDay,\ninternal/config/render.go:194:\t\t\tTokensPerDay:    role.TokensPerDay,\ninternal/config/tokens.go:13:// TokenCount is a token amount that unmarshals from a plain integer or a\ninternal/config/tokens.go:14:// string such as \"40M\", \"1.5M\" or \"500k\" (see ParseTokenCount).\ninternal/config/tokens.go:15:type TokenCount int64\ninternal/config/tokens.go:19:// ParseTokenCount parses a positive whole number of tokens: digits with an\ninternal/config/tokens.go:23:func ParseTokenCount(s string) (int64, error) {\ninternal/config/tokens.go:62:func (t TokenCount) String() string { return strconv.FormatInt(int64(t), 10) }\ninternal/config/tokens.go:65:func (t *TokenCount) UnmarshalYAML(value *yaml.Node) error {\ninternal/config/tokens.go:74:\t\tn, err := ParseTokenCount(value.Value)\ninternal/config/tokens.go:78:\t\t*t = TokenCount(n)\ninternal/config/tokens.go:86:func (t TokenCount) MarshalYAML() (any, error) { return int64(t), nil }\ninternal/config/types.go:167:\t// TokensPerDay is the role's own daily token cap; 0 means unset.\ninternal/config/types.go:168:\tTokensPerDay int64\ninternal/config/types.go:214:\tTokensPerDay    int64   // default per-role daily token cap; 0 = no token cap\ninternal/config/types.go:250:// RoleTokensPerDay is the role's daily token cap: its own value, else the\ninternal/config/types.go:251:// repo-wide Resolved.TokensPerDay. set is false when neither is set (no cap).\ninternal/config/types.go:252:func (r *Resolved) RoleTokensPerDay(role Role) (cap int64, set bool) {\ninternal/config/types.go:253:\tif role.TokensPerDay > 0 {\ninternal/config/types.go:254:\t\treturn role.TokensPerDay, true\ninternal/config/types.go:256:\tif r.TokensPerDay > 0 {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2168eb67-7a3e-48bf-9b05-6a957a8a97c0","uuid":"0b37ca80-cf40-4ec7-882d-edefb4512a3f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:01:27.777Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nThis adds the daily token check to the pool's claim gate. A job must now pass both the dollar check and the token check. It also adds a once-per-day status-issue notice for each token cap. Both dependencies have landed on main: the dollar gate and its notice loop are in internal/budget, and the token config is in internal/config. The work can start now, and engineer is the only triage role in this repository.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: implementation steps for the token check in internal/budget, wiring it into the existing dollar gate and verdict, the token notice and report, the proposal doc updates, and table tests on a fake clock.\n- worker engineer: Go code, tests and doc changes in internal/budget, the pool wiring and docs/proposal.md.\n\n## Open issues\n- The issue asks for a human review of the claim-rule table and the fail-closed path. eng-review runs on every pull request, but a maintainer should still review those parts of the pull request.\n- No architect or documentation-planner role exists. The engineer's plan has to cover how this fits with the existing dollar gate and notice loop, and the changes to the proposal's Budgets, Configuration, Executors and Reaper sections.\nbudget.go\nbudget_test.go\nnotice.go\nnotice_test.go\ntestdata\n     168 internal/budget/budget.go\n     137 internal/budget/budget_test.go\n     163 internal/budget/notice.go\n     227 internal/budget/notice_test.go\n     695 total\n# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\ninternal/config/defaults.go:132:\t\t\tres.TokensPerDay = int64(*raw.tokensPerDay)\ninternal/config/duration.go:18:// durationToken matches one number-plus-unit component of a duration.\ninternal/config/duration.go:19:var durationToken = regexp.MustCompile(`^([0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]+)?)(ns|us|µs|ms|s|m|h|d|w)`)\ninternal/config/duration.go:35:\t\tm := durationToken.FindStringSubmatch(rest)\ninternal/config/load.go:323:\t\t\tvar tc TokenCount\ninternal/config/load.go:417:\t\trole.TokensPerDay = *ov.tokensPerDay\ninternal/config/raw.go:23:\ttokensPerDay           *TokenCount\ninternal/config/render.go:29:\tTokensPerDay    int64                  `yaml:\"tokens_per_day,omitempty\"`\ninternal/config/render.go:120:\tTokensPerDay    int64   `yaml:\"tokens_per_day,omitempty\"`\ninternal/config/render.go:137:\t\tTokensPerDay:    r.TokensPerDay,\ninternal/config/render.go:194:\t\t\tTokensPerDay:    role.TokensPerDay,\ninternal/config/tokens.go:13:// TokenCount is a token amount that unmarshals from a plain integer or a\ninternal/config/tokens.go:14:// string such as \"40M\", \"1.5M\" or \"500k\" (see ParseTokenCount).\ninternal/config/tokens.go:15:type TokenCount int64\ninternal/config/tokens.go:19:// ParseTokenCount parses a positive whole number of tokens: digits with an\ninternal/config/tokens.go:23:func ParseTokenCount(s string) (int64, error) {\ninternal/config/tokens.go:62:func (t TokenCount) String() string { return strconv.FormatInt(int64(t), 10) }\ninternal/config/tokens.go:65:func (t *TokenCount) UnmarshalYAML(value *yaml.Node) error {\ninternal/config/tokens.go:74:\t\tn, err := ParseTokenCount(value.Value)\ninternal/config/tokens.go:78:\t\t*t = TokenCount(n)\ninternal/config/tokens.go:86:func (t TokenCount) MarshalYAML() (any, error) { return int64(t), nil }\ninternal/config/types.go:167:\t// TokensPerDay is the role's own daily token cap; 0 means unset.\ninternal/config/types.go:168:\tTokensPerDay int64\ninternal/config/types.go:214:\tTokensPerDay    int64   // default per-role daily token cap; 0 = no token cap\ninternal/config/types.go:250:// RoleTokensPerDay is the role's daily token cap: its own value, else the\ninternal/config/types.go:251:// repo-wide Resolved.TokensPerDay. set is false when neither is set (no cap).\ninternal/config/types.go:252:func (r *Resolved) RoleTokensPerDay(role Role) (cap int64, set bool) {\ninternal/config/types.go:253:\tif role.TokensPerDay > 0 {\ninternal/config/types.go:254:\t\treturn role.TokensPerDay, true\ninternal/config/types.go:256:\tif r.TokensPerDay > 0 {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E5c7eVCDYPhfd7qVeLp8Xm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNWLEG1ocqW5dhthxL5J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XKoHrWLsyCw8DvvmvUWDJq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat internal/budget/budget.go; sed -n 1,163p internal/budget/notice.go; grep -rn \"budget\\.\" --include=*.go . | grep -v \"^./internal/budget\" | head -20; grep -n \"Worst\\|min_remaining\\|WorstCase\\|tokens_window\\|TokenWindow\" -r internal/config/types.go docs/proposal.md | head -20; grep -n \"^## \\|^### \" docs/proposal.md | grep -i \"budget\\|config\\|executor\\|reaper\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2506,"cache_read_input_tokens":10660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2506},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2168eb67-7a3e-48bf-9b05-6a957a8a97c0","uuid":"cdaf99e8-eafd-4007-b432-a5ac6d9cd7e3","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:01:29.639Z","request_id":"req_011ChNWLE7bF7fNaTQRBAEgx"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XKoHrWLsyCw8DvvmvUWDJq","type":"tool_result","content":"// Package budget enforces the daily dollar caps at the pool's claim gate.\n//\n// The day is the UTC day. A candidate is refused when spent >= cap, for its\n// role's own cap (budget_usd_per_day on the role) or the repo cap. Steps that\n// reported no cost count as $0 and their number is shown. Reviewers get no\n// exemption; deterministic scanners cost nothing and are exempt. A job that\n// already holds a slot is never touched: the gate only sees new candidates.\n// A state read failure denies (fails closed).\npackage budget\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/pool\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n)\n\n// SpendReader reads today's spend; *state.Store satisfies it.\ntype SpendReader interface {\n\tSpendSince(ctx context.Context, dayStart time.Time) (map[state.RoleKey]state.Spend, state.Spend, error)\n}\n\n// Gate is the pool's Options.Budget hook.\ntype Gate struct {\n\tstore SpendReader\n\tcfg   func() *config.Resolved\n\tnow   func() time.Time\n\tlog   *slog.Logger\n\n\tmu     sync.Mutex\n\tday    time.Time       // UTC day start the logged map belongs to\n\tlogged map[string]bool // caps already logged on day\n}\n\n// New builds a Gate. cfg returns the latest config (nil: nothing is capped);\n// now nil means time.Now; log nil means slog.Default.\nfunc New(store SpendReader, cfg func() *config.Resolved, now func() time.Time, log *slog.Logger) *Gate {\n\tif now == nil {\n\t\tnow = time.Now\n\t}\n\tif log == nil {\n\t\tlog = slog.Default()\n\t}\n\treturn &Gate{store: store, cfg: cfg, now: now, log: log, logged: map[string]bool{}}\n}\n\nfunc kindOf(c pool.Class) (config.Kind, string, bool) {\n\tswitch c {\n\tcase pool.ClassScanner:\n\t\treturn config.KindScanner, c.String(), true\n\tcase pool.ClassTriage:\n\t\treturn config.KindTriage, c.String(), true\n\tcase pool.ClassWorker:\n\t\treturn config.KindWorker, c.String(), true\n\tcase pool.ClassReview:\n\t\treturn config.KindReviewer, c.String(), true\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", \"\", false\n}\n\n// Denied reports whether a cap forbids starting c, and why.\nfunc (g *Gate) Denied(c pool.Candidate) (bool, string) {\n\tkind, stage, ok := kindOf(c.Class)\n\tif !ok {\n\t\treturn false, \"\"\n\t}\n\tcfg := g.cfg()\n\tif cfg == nil {\n\t\treturn false, \"\"\n\t}\n\trole, ok := cfg.Role(kind, c.Role)\n\tif !ok || (kind == config.KindScanner && role.ScanPath != \"\") {\n\t\treturn false, \"\"\n\t}\n\tdayStart := utcDayStart(g.now())\n\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Second)\n\tdefer cancel()\n\tper, repo, err := g.store.SpendSince(ctx, dayStart)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tg.log.Error(\"budget.read_failed\", \"error\", err)\n\t\treturn true, \"budget: spend unreadable, failing closed\"\n\t}\n\tif cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay > 0 && repo.USD >= cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay {\n\t\treturn true, g.capped(dayStart, \"repo\", \"\", repo, cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay)\n\t}\n\tif limit, set := cfg.RoleBudgetUSDPerDay(role); set {\n\t\tsp := per[state.RoleKey{Stage: stage, Role: c.Role}]\n\t\tif sp.USD >= limit {\n\t\t\treturn true, g.capped(dayStart, \"role\", stage+\"/\"+c.Role, sp, limit)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false, \"\"\n}\n\n// capped builds the reason and logs budget.capped once per cap and UTC day.\nfunc (g *Gate) capped(dayStart time.Time, scope, role string, sp state.Spend, limit float64) string {\n\treason := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s daily budget reached: $%.2f of $%.2f spent today (UTC)\", scope, sp.USD, limit)\n\tif sp.Unpriced > 0 {\n\t\treason += fmt.Sprintf(\", %d unpriced steps counted as $0\", sp.Unpriced)\n\t}\n\tg.mu.Lock()\n\tif !g.day.Equal(dayStart) {\n\t\tg.day, g.logged = dayStart, map[string]bool{}\n\t}\n\tkey := scope + \"|\" + role\n\tfirst := !g.logged[key]\n\tg.logged[key] = true\n\tg.mu.Unlock()\n\tif first {\n\t\tg.log.Warn(\"budget.capped\", \"scope\", scope, \"role\", role, \"spent_usd\", sp.USD, \"cap_usd\", limit, \"unpriced\", sp.Unpriced)\n\t}\n\treturn reason\n}\n\n// utcDayStart is 00:00 UTC of t's UTC day: the one day rule of the gate and\n// the notice loop.\nfunc utcDayStart(t time.Time) time.Time {\n\tt = t.UTC()\n\treturn time.Date(t.Year(), t.Month(), t.Day(), 0, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)\n}\n\n// Cap is one reached cap. Scope is \"repo\" or \"role\"; Stage and Role are empty\n// for the repo cap.\ntype Cap struct {\n\tScope, Stage, Role string\n\tSpent              state.Spend\n\tLimit              float64\n}\n\n// Capped returns every cap reached today (repo first, then roles in config\n// order) and the UTC day start. It applies the rules of Denied, logs nothing.\nfunc (g *Gate) Capped(ctx context.Context) ([]Cap, time.Time, error) {\n\tdayStart := utcDayStart(g.now())\n\tcfg := g.cfg()\n\tif cfg == nil {\n\t\treturn nil, dayStart, nil\n\t}\n\tper, repo, err := g.store.SpendSince(ctx, dayStart)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, dayStart, err\n\t}\n\tvar out []Cap\n\tif cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay > 0 && repo.USD >= cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay {\n\t\tout = append(out, Cap{Scope: \"repo\", Spent: repo, Limit: cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay})\n\t}\n\tstages := map[config.Kind]string{config.KindScanner: \"scanner\", config.KindTriage: \"triage\", config.KindWorker: \"worker\", config.KindReviewer: \"review\"}\n\tfor _, role := range cfg.Roles {\n\t\tif role.Kind == config.KindScanner && role.ScanPath != \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tstage, ok := stages[role.Kind]\n\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif limit, set := cfg.RoleBudgetUSDPerDay(role); set {\n\t\t\tsp := per[state.RoleKey{Stage: stage, Role: role.Name}]\n\t\t\tif sp.USD >= limit {\n\t\t\t\tout = append(out, Cap{Scope: \"role\", Stage: stage, Role: role.Name, Spent: sp, Limit: limit})\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn out, dayStart, nil\n}\npackage budget\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n)\n\n// Name is the notice loop's name, as --loops spells it.\nconst Name = \"budget\"\n\n// Capper lists the caps reached today; *Gate satisfies it.\ntype Capper interface {\n\tCapped(ctx context.Context) ([]Cap, time.Time, error)\n}\n\n// EventStore is the part of *state.Store the loop uses.\ntype EventStore interface {\n\tAppendEvent(ctx context.Context, e state.Event) error\n\tEvents(ctx context.Context, f state.EventFilter) ([]state.Event, error)\n}\n\n// Effects is the part of effects.Effects the loop uses.\ntype Effects interface {\n\tCreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error)\n\tDryRun() bool\n}\n\n// Deps are the loop's collaborators. StatusIssue returns 0 until the status\n// issue is known. Now nil means time.Now; Log nil means slog.Default.\ntype Deps struct {\n\tGate        Capper\n\tStore       EventStore\n\tEffects     Effects\n\tStatusIssue func() int\n\tLog         *slog.Logger\n\tNow         func() time.Time\n}\n\n// Loop posts one status-issue comment per reached cap and UTC day. A\n// budget_capped event written after the comment is the record for #58 and the\n// marker that keeps a restart from posting the notice again.\ntype Loop struct {\n\td  Deps\n\tmu sync.Mutex\n}\n\n// NewLoop builds the notice loop.\nfunc NewLoop(d Deps) *Loop {\n\tif d.Now == nil {\n\t\td.Now = time.Now\n\t}\n\tif d.Log == nil {\n\t\td.Log = slog.Default()\n\t}\n\treturn &Loop{d: d}\n}\n\n// Name implements controller.Loop.\nfunc (*Loop) Name() string { return Name }\n\n// Interval implements controller.Loop.\nfunc (*Loop) Interval(*config.Resolved) time.Duration { return time.Minute }\n\n// Claims is false: the notice is bookkeeping about work already done.\nfunc (*Loop) Claims() bool { return false }\n\nvar _ controller.Loop = (*Loop)(nil)\n\ntype noticeKey struct{ scope, stage, role, day string }\n\n// Tick posts the notices that are due.\nfunc (l *Loop) Tick(ctx context.Context, _ controller.Env) error {\n\tl.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer l.mu.Unlock()\n\tissue := l.d.StatusIssue()\n\tif issue == 0 {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tcaps, dayStart, err := l.d.Gate.Capped(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"budget: read spend: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif len(caps) == 0 {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tday := dayStart.Format(\"2006-01-02\")\n\tevs, err := l.d.Store.Events(ctx, state.EventFilter{Kind: state.EventBudgetCapped, Since: dayStart})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"budget: read events: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tdone := map[noticeKey]bool{}\n\tfor _, e := range evs {\n\t\tvar d struct {\n\t\t\tScope string `json:\"scope\"`\n\t\t\tDay   string `json:\"day\"`\n\t\t}\n\t\tif json.Unmarshal(e.Data, &d) == nil {\n\t\t\tdone[noticeKey{d.Scope, e.Stage, e.Role, d.Day}] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor _, c := range caps {\n\t\tif done[noticeKey{c.Scope, c.Stage, c.Role, day}] {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, err := l.d.Effects.CreateComment(ctx, issue, Render(c, day)); err != nil {\n\t\t\tl.d.Log.Error(\"budget.notice_failed\", \"scope\", c.Scope, \"stage\", c.Stage, \"role\", c.Role, \"error\", err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tdata, _ := json.Marshal(map[string]any{\n\t\t\t\"scope\": c.Scope, \"stage\": c.Stage, \"role\": c.Role, \"day\": day,\n\t\t\t\"spent_usd\": c.Spent.USD, \"cap_usd\": c.Limit, \"unpriced\": c.Spent.Unpriced,\n\t\t})\n\t\tev := state.Event{At: l.d.Now(), Kind: state.EventBudgetCapped, Stage: c.Stage, Role: c.Role, Data: data}\n\t\tif err := l.d.Store.AppendEvent(ctx, ev); err != nil {\n\t\t\tl.d.Log.Error(\"budget.notice_unrecorded\", \"scope\", c.Scope, \"stage\", c.Stage, \"role\", c.Role, \"error\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nvar safeName = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z0-9._/-]+$`)\n\nfunc safe(s string) string {\n\tif safeName.MatchString(s) {\n\t\treturn s\n\t}\n\treturn \"?\"\n}\n\n// Render is the comment for c on the UTC day (2006-01-02). It holds only\n// numbers, the day and config names; no agent text and no \"@\".\nfunc Render(c Cap, day string) string {\n\tvar b strings.Builder\n\twhat := \"The repo's daily budget\"\n\twhere := \"the repo-wide `budget_usd_per_day`\"\n\tscope := \"repo\"\n\tif c.Scope == \"role\" {\n\t\tstage, role := safe(c.Stage), safe(c.Role)\n\t\twhat = fmt.Sprintf(\"The daily budget of %s role `%s`\", stage, role)\n\t\twhere = fmt.Sprintf(\"`budget_usd_per_day` of role `%s` (or the repo-wide value)\", role)\n\t\tscope = \"role \" + stage + \"/\" + role\n\t}\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"<!-- ard:budget scope=%s day=%s -->\\n\", strings.ReplaceAll(scope, \" \", \"-\"), day)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"**ard · daily budget reached**\\n\\n\")\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"%s is reached for %s (UTC): $%.2f of $%.2f spent.\", what, day, c.Spent.USD, c.Limit)\n\tif c.Spent.Unpriced > 0 {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \" %d steps reported no cost and count as $0.\", c.Spent.Unpriced)\n\t}\n\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\\nNo new jobs start under this cap; running jobs finish. On a subscription the dollar figure is an estimate.\\n\\n\")\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"To raise the cap, change %s in `.ard/config.yaml` through a reviewed pull request. The cap clears at 00:00 UTC.\\n\", where)\n\treturn b.String()\n}\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\n286:## Executors and the Reaper\n424:## Configuration","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2168eb67-7a3e-48bf-9b05-6a957a8a97c0","uuid":"1c6ebda3-856e-41ca-b5f4-b93f4c5da6ca","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:01:29.707Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// Package budget enforces the daily dollar caps at the pool's claim gate.\n//\n// The day is the UTC day. A candidate is refused when spent >= cap, for its\n// role's own cap (budget_usd_per_day on the role) or the repo cap. Steps that\n// reported no cost count as $0 and their number is shown. Reviewers get no\n// exemption; deterministic scanners cost nothing and are exempt. A job that\n// already holds a slot is never touched: the gate only sees new candidates.\n// A state read failure denies (fails closed).\npackage budget\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/pool\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n)\n\n// SpendReader reads today's spend; *state.Store satisfies it.\ntype SpendReader interface {\n\tSpendSince(ctx context.Context, dayStart time.Time) (map[state.RoleKey]state.Spend, state.Spend, error)\n}\n\n// Gate is the pool's Options.Budget hook.\ntype Gate struct {\n\tstore SpendReader\n\tcfg   func() *config.Resolved\n\tnow   func() time.Time\n\tlog   *slog.Logger\n\n\tmu     sync.Mutex\n\tday    time.Time       // UTC day start the logged map belongs to\n\tlogged map[string]bool // caps already logged on day\n}\n\n// New builds a Gate. cfg returns the latest config (nil: nothing is capped);\n// now nil means time.Now; log nil means slog.Default.\nfunc New(store SpendReader, cfg func() *config.Resolved, now func() time.Time, log *slog.Logger) *Gate {\n\tif now == nil {\n\t\tnow = time.Now\n\t}\n\tif log == nil {\n\t\tlog = slog.Default()\n\t}\n\treturn &Gate{store: store, cfg: cfg, now: now, log: log, logged: map[string]bool{}}\n}\n\nfunc kindOf(c pool.Class) (config.Kind, string, bool) {\n\tswitch c {\n\tcase pool.ClassScanner:\n\t\treturn config.KindScanner, c.String(), true\n\tcase pool.ClassTriage:\n\t\treturn config.KindTriage, c.String(), true\n\tcase pool.ClassWorker:\n\t\treturn config.KindWorker, c.String(), true\n\tcase pool.ClassReview:\n\t\treturn config.KindReviewer, c.String(), true\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", \"\", false\n}\n\n// Denied reports whether a cap forbids starting c, and why.\nfunc (g *Gate) Denied(c pool.Candidate) (bool, string) {\n\tkind, stage, ok := kindOf(c.Class)\n\tif !ok {\n\t\treturn false, \"\"\n\t}\n\tcfg := g.cfg()\n\tif cfg == nil {\n\t\treturn false, \"\"\n\t}\n\trole, ok := cfg.Role(kind, c.Role)\n\tif !ok || (kind == config.KindScanner && role.ScanPath != \"\") {\n\t\treturn false, \"\"\n\t}\n\tdayStart := utcDayStart(g.now())\n\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Second)\n\tdefer cancel()\n\tper, repo, err := g.store.SpendSince(ctx, dayStart)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tg.log.Error(\"budget.read_failed\", \"error\", err)\n\t\treturn true, \"budget: spend unreadable, failing closed\"\n\t}\n\tif cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay > 0 && repo.USD >= cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay {\n\t\treturn true, g.capped(dayStart, \"repo\", \"\", repo, cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay)\n\t}\n\tif limit, set := cfg.RoleBudgetUSDPerDay(role); set {\n\t\tsp := per[state.RoleKey{Stage: stage, Role: c.Role}]\n\t\tif sp.USD >= limit {\n\t\t\treturn true, g.capped(dayStart, \"role\", stage+\"/\"+c.Role, sp, limit)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false, \"\"\n}\n\n// capped builds the reason and logs budget.capped once per cap and UTC day.\nfunc (g *Gate) capped(dayStart time.Time, scope, role string, sp state.Spend, limit float64) string {\n\treason := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s daily budget reached: $%.2f of $%.2f spent today (UTC)\", scope, sp.USD, limit)\n\tif sp.Unpriced > 0 {\n\t\treason += fmt.Sprintf(\", %d unpriced steps counted as $0\", sp.Unpriced)\n\t}\n\tg.mu.Lock()\n\tif !g.day.Equal(dayStart) {\n\t\tg.day, g.logged = dayStart, map[string]bool{}\n\t}\n\tkey := scope + \"|\" + role\n\tfirst := !g.logged[key]\n\tg.logged[key] = true\n\tg.mu.Unlock()\n\tif first {\n\t\tg.log.Warn(\"budget.capped\", \"scope\", scope, \"role\", role, \"spent_usd\", sp.USD, \"cap_usd\", limit, \"unpriced\", sp.Unpriced)\n\t}\n\treturn reason\n}\n\n// utcDayStart is 00:00 UTC of t's UTC day: the one day rule of the gate and\n// the notice loop.\nfunc utcDayStart(t time.Time) time.Time {\n\tt = t.UTC()\n\treturn time.Date(t.Year(), t.Month(), t.Day(), 0, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)\n}\n\n// Cap is one reached cap. Scope is \"repo\" or \"role\"; Stage and Role are empty\n// for the repo cap.\ntype Cap struct {\n\tScope, Stage, Role string\n\tSpent              state.Spend\n\tLimit              float64\n}\n\n// Capped returns every cap reached today (repo first, then roles in config\n// order) and the UTC day start. It applies the rules of Denied, logs nothing.\nfunc (g *Gate) Capped(ctx context.Context) ([]Cap, time.Time, error) {\n\tdayStart := utcDayStart(g.now())\n\tcfg := g.cfg()\n\tif cfg == nil {\n\t\treturn nil, dayStart, nil\n\t}\n\tper, repo, err := g.store.SpendSince(ctx, dayStart)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, dayStart, err\n\t}\n\tvar out []Cap\n\tif cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay > 0 && repo.USD >= cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay {\n\t\tout = append(out, Cap{Scope: \"repo\", Spent: repo, Limit: cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay})\n\t}\n\tstages := map[config.Kind]string{config.KindScanner: \"scanner\", config.KindTriage: \"triage\", config.KindWorker: \"worker\", config.KindReviewer: \"review\"}\n\tfor _, role := range cfg.Roles {\n\t\tif role.Kind == config.KindScanner && role.ScanPath != \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tstage, ok := stages[role.Kind]\n\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif limit, set := cfg.RoleBudgetUSDPerDay(role); set {\n\t\t\tsp := per[state.RoleKey{Stage: stage, Role: role.Name}]\n\t\t\tif sp.USD >= limit {\n\t\t\t\tout = append(out, Cap{Scope: \"role\", Stage: stage, Role: role.Name, Spent: sp, Limit: limit})\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn out, dayStart, nil\n}\npackage budget\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n)\n\n// Name is the notice loop's name, as --loops spells it.\nconst Name = \"budget\"\n\n// Capper lists the caps reached today; *Gate satisfies it.\ntype Capper interface {\n\tCapped(ctx context.Context) ([]Cap, time.Time, error)\n}\n\n// EventStore is the part of *state.Store the loop uses.\ntype EventStore interface {\n\tAppendEvent(ctx context.Context, e state.Event) error\n\tEvents(ctx context.Context, f state.EventFilter) ([]state.Event, error)\n}\n\n// Effects is the part of effects.Effects the loop uses.\ntype Effects interface {\n\tCreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error)\n\tDryRun() bool\n}\n\n// Deps are the loop's collaborators. StatusIssue returns 0 until the status\n// issue is known. Now nil means time.Now; Log nil means slog.Default.\ntype Deps struct {\n\tGate        Capper\n\tStore       EventStore\n\tEffects     Effects\n\tStatusIssue func() int\n\tLog         *slog.Logger\n\tNow         func() time.Time\n}\n\n// Loop posts one status-issue comment per reached cap and UTC day. A\n// budget_capped event written after the comment is the record for #58 and the\n// marker that keeps a restart from posting the notice again.\ntype Loop struct {\n\td  Deps\n\tmu sync.Mutex\n}\n\n// NewLoop builds the notice loop.\nfunc NewLoop(d Deps) *Loop {\n\tif d.Now == nil {\n\t\td.Now = time.Now\n\t}\n\tif d.Log == nil {\n\t\td.Log = slog.Default()\n\t}\n\treturn &Loop{d: d}\n}\n\n// Name implements controller.Loop.\nfunc (*Loop) Name() string { return Name }\n\n// Interval implements controller.Loop.\nfunc (*Loop) Interval(*config.Resolved) time.Duration { return time.Minute }\n\n// Claims is false: the notice is bookkeeping about work already done.\nfunc (*Loop) Claims() bool { return false }\n\nvar _ controller.Loop = (*Loop)(nil)\n\ntype noticeKey struct{ scope, stage, role, day string }\n\n// Tick posts the notices that are due.\nfunc (l *Loop) Tick(ctx context.Context, _ controller.Env) error {\n\tl.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer l.mu.Unlock()\n\tissue := l.d.StatusIssue()\n\tif issue == 0 {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tcaps, dayStart, err := l.d.Gate