) is mounted from the config snapshot at the job's SHA, not from the working tree. The job worktree is always detached at a SHA resolved from the job's ref (the executor never checks out a branch; the committer owns branch worktrees). T\n\nA worker job is several executor jobs (`<id>`, `<id>t1`, `<id>f1`, ...) under one state job and one slot; the Reaper watches whichever step is stored on the job, so its heartbeat and deadline rules apply to tests too.\n\n**One pool of job slots, drained from the end.** At most `max_pods` jobs (default 3) run at once, shared by every loop. When a slot frees, the controller fills it in this order: reviewers, then workers, then triage, then scanners, oldest first within each. Finishing work in flight beats starting new\n\n|  | Local executor | Kubernetes executor |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Workspace | `git worktree` of the controller's clone (`~/.ard/repos/<owner>/<repo>.git`) under `~/.ard/work/<owner>/<repo>/<job-id>`; sidecar exported into the job home | a bare Pod whose `pre` init container fetches the repo at `BaseSHA` with a per-job read-only installation token and runs the sa\n| Runtime | the role's `Dockerfile` image under Docker if it has one, else the `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE` default image when set and the role reads untrusted input, else a host subprocess; hard timeout | a bare Pod (no Job object): init `pre`, isolated `agent` container (default `ard-agent` image) under `ard\n| Heartbeat | PID alive plus log file mtime | the controller follows the agent's `pods/log` into the host log; log mtime |\n9:test:\n20:# run by the ard-ci pipeline, not part of `make test`).\n25:# network; not part of `make test`).\n30:# ID. Local only, never published. Needs Docker and network; not part of `make test`.\n35:# Checks ard-agent:dev (needs Docker; run `make agent-image` first; not part of `make test`).\n40:# Needs Docker and network; not part of `make test`.\n47:# internal/roles/testdata/lts/regen.sh). Needs Docker and network; not part of `make test`.\n54:# internal/roles/testdata/lint/regen.sh). Needs Docker; not part of `make test`.\n61:# docs/site/requirements.txt) and runs the docs drift test (part of `make test`).\n67:# (needs goreleaser v2 and python3; not part of `make test`).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2168eb67-7a3e-48bf-9b05-6a957a8a97c0","uuid":"61d586fd-31b4-4a60-8d2b-14539966ddd0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:01:37.828Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"internal/servecmd/serve.go:300:\t\t\t\tp, err := adoptPool(ctx, store, w.MaxPods, log, w.limitedFor, w.budgetGate().Denied)\ninternal/servecmd/budget.go:13:func (w *wiring) budgetGate() *budget.Gate {\ninternal/servecmd/budget.go:30:\t\tGate: w.budgetGate(), Store: w.Store, Effects: w.Effects,\ninternal/pool/demand.go:22:\t\t\t\tdelete(p.firstDenied, k)\ninternal/pool/demand.go:82:\t\t\t\tdelete(p.firstDenied, k)\ninternal/pool/demand.go:90:\t\tif _, ok := p.firstDenied[k]; !ok {\ninternal/pool/demand.go:91:\t\t\tp.firstDenied[k] = now\ninternal/pool/demand.go:107:\t\t\tif t, ok := p.firstDenied[k]; ok && now.Sub(t) > w.oldest {\ninternal/pool/pool.go:83:\tfirstDenied map[string]time.Time\ninternal/pool/pool.go:98:\t\tfirstDenied: map[string]time.Time{},\ninternal/state/events.go:38:\t// EventBudgetCapped: the budget loop posted the status-issue notice for a\ninternal/state/events.go:42:\tEventBudgetCapped = \"budget_capped\"\n17:type fakeReader struct {\n24:func (f *fakeReader) SpendSince(_ context.Context, d time.Time) (map[state.RoleKey]state.Spend, state.Spend, error) {\n29:func testCfg() *config.Resolved {\n39:func cand(c pool.Class, role string) pool.Candidate {\n43:func setup(r *fakeReader) (*Gate, *bytes.Buffer, *time.Time) {\n50:func TestRoleCap(t *testing.T) {\n69:func TestRepoCap(t *testing.T) {\n84:func TestReaderErrorFailsClosed(t *testing.T) {\n94:func TestCappedLoggedOncePerDay(t *testing.T) {\n109:func TestCapped(t *testing.T) {\n## Executors and the Reaper\n\nAn executor runs one agent job somewhere